From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Read the PS5 signal frame's FP state at its measured offset.

Wine found a signal's FXSAVE image at mcontext_t's mc_fpstate, which with
patch 0500's mcontext at ucontext+64 is ucontext+288. The PS5 kernel keeps
32 more bytes in its mcontext than the SDK header declares. A payload that
loads known values into MXCSR, XMM0-15 and the YMM upper halves and then
faults found FXSAVE at +320 (XMM0 at +480, MXCSR 0x9fc0 as loaded), the
XSAVE header at +832 (XSTATE_BV 7) and the YMM upper halves at +896.
At +288 there are two pointers and a zero where MXCSR would be. Values the
handler wrote at +320 were restored by sigreturn.

So an exception's CONTEXT carried MXCSR 0 (all FP exceptions unmasked) and
XMM registers shifted by two, and a handler that resumed execution through
NtContinue or an unwind loaded them. Read FXSAVE at +320 and expose the
extended state that follows it. PS5_Proton found the same offset
(mihawk-99, its patch 0800).

  dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c | 10 ++++++++++
  1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index d17b306..ee77208 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -296,8 +296,18 @@ __ASM_GLOBAL_FUNC( modify_ldt,
 #define RSP_sig(context)     (UCONTEXT_MC(context).mc_rsp)
 #define TRAP_sig(context)    (UCONTEXT_MC(context).mc_trapno)
 #define ERROR_sig(context)   (UCONTEXT_MC(context).mc_err)
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+/* Measured on PS5 FW 12.02 with a payload that faults with known FP state:
+ * the kernel keeps 32 more bytes in mcontext_t than the SDK header declares,
+ * so its FXSAVE image is at ucontext offset 320, not mc_fpstate (288), and
+ * sigreturn restores MXCSR and XMM from there. The XSAVE header follows at
+ * 832 and the YMM upper halves at 896, in the standard (uncompacted) form. */
+#define FPU_sig(context)     ((void *)((char *)(context) + 320))
+#define XState_sig(fpu)      ((XSAVE_AREA_HEADER *)((char *)(fpu) + sizeof(XSAVE_FORMAT)))
+#else
 #define FPU_sig(context)     ((void *)(UCONTEXT_MC(context).mc_fpstate))
 #define XState_sig(context)  NULL
+#endif
 
 #elif defined(__NetBSD__)
 
